        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="wOb7pYrqCbg5zpdAHGhP-10" value="page title clearly identifies the purpose of the page, allowing users to immediately understand that they are logging into a pre existing account" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1010" y="-230" width="170" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="wOb7pYrqCbg5zpdAHGhP-11" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;rounded=0;" parent="1" target="ItLBluMeHKCG-IMd_qxg-25" edge="1">
          <mxGeometry width="50" height="50" relative="1" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint x="970" y="690" as="sourcePoint" />
            <mxPoint x="930" y="760" as="targetPoint" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="wOb7pYrqCbg5zpdAHGhP-12" value="page title clearly identifies the purpose of the page, allowing users to immediately understand that they are creating a new account" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="970" y="660" width="160" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="wOb7pYrqCbg5zpdAHGhP-17" value="The name input box allows users to enter their name when creating an account. It is clearly labelled so that users understand what information is required. Collecting the user&#39;s name allows the fitness tracker to personalise the experience, such as displaying a welcome message on the dashboard." style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="620" y="630" width="245" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="wOb7pYrqCbg5zpdAHGhP-19" value="The email input box allows users to enter their email address. This information can be used to identify their account and potentially support future account recovery features. " style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1245" y="1030" width="175" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="wOb7pYrqCbg5zpdAHGhP-23" value="The date of birth input allows users to enter their date of birth when creating an account. This information can be used to personalise the fitness tracker and could support future features that calculate age-related fitness information." style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="90" y="970" width="230" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="wOb7pYrqCbg5zpdAHGhP-25" value="The navigation bar is positioned at the top of the page to provide users with easy access to the main features of the fitness tracker.This makes the application easier to navigate because users can move between different sections" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1070" y="1250" width="230" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="wOb7pYrqCbg5zpdAHGhP-27" value="The daily steps graph provides a visual representation of the user&#39;s step count over time. A graph is used because it allows users to identify trends and compare their activity across different days more easily than reading individual numbers. This improves the usability of the fitness tracker by making fitness data easier to understand." style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="90" y="1580" width="290" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="wOb7pYrqCbg5zpdAHGhP-29" value="The workout graph shows the user&#39;s workout activity over time. A graph is appropriate because it allows users to identify patterns in their exercise routine, such as whether they are completing more workouts each week. This can help users evaluate their consistency and stay motivated to maintain their fitness routine." style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1320" y="1580" width="260" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Y4wUbL-xrpzmWVxsvZfx-1" value="The calories graph provides a visual representation of the user&#39;s calorie data over time. This makes it easier for users to compare their calorie intake across different days and identify patterns in their activity. A graph improves the presentation of this information by making trends easier to recognise." style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1090" y="1970" width="300" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Y4wUbL-xrpzmWVxsvZfx-3" value="The weight graph displays changes in the user&#39;s recorded weight over time. A graph is used because it makes trends easier to identify than displaying individual measurements. For example, users can see whether their weight has remained consistent or changed over a period of time. This supports the fitness tracker&#39;s purpose of helping users monitor their progress and understand their fitness habits." style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="460" y="2000" width="300" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Y4wUbL-xrpzmWVxsvZfx-5" value="The navigation bar is positioned at the top of the page to provide users with easy access to the main features of the fitness tracker.This makes the application easier to navigate because users can move between different sections" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2300" y="1830" width="210" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Y4wUbL-xrpzmWVxsvZfx-7" value="The Weight button allows users to record their weight measurements. A separate button is used to make this feature easy to find and access without requiring users to navigate through a complicated form. When selected, an overlay appears where the user can enter their weight and the date it was recorded. This makes the process of recording weight simple and efficient." style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2490" y="2170" width="300" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Y4wUbL-xrpzmWVxsvZfx-9" value="The Workout button allows users to record information about their exercise activities. This is useful because users may participate in different types of workouts and want to monitor their exercise habits. When selected, an overlay appears where the user can enter the workout type, duration and date. Separating workouts from other fitness data makes the interface more organised and ensures that the user is only asked to enter information relevant to their activity." style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1710" y="1760" width="350" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Y4wUbL-xrpzmWVxsvZfx-11" value="The Calories button allows users to record their calorie information. When selected, an overlay appears with input fields for calories consumed, calories burned and the date. Providing a separate form makes it easier for users to enter the correct information and reduces confusion between different types of fitness data." style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1620" y="2440" width="310" height="110" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Y4wUbL-xrpzmWVxsvZfx-13" value="The Steps button allows users to record their daily step count. This is important because step count is a useful measurement of daily physical activity. When selected, an overlay appears where the user can enter their step count and the date. A separate button makes this feature easy to access and allows users to quickly record their daily activity." style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2320" y="2480" width="270" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Y4wUbL-xrpzmWVxsvZfx-15" value="The navigation bar is positioned at the top of the page to provide users with easy access to the main features of the fitness tracker.This makes the application easier to navigate because users can move between different sections" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1010" y="2350" width="250" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Y4wUbL-xrpzmWVxsvZfx-16" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;rounded=0;" parent="1" edge="1">
          <mxGeometry width="50" height="50" relative="1" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint x="330" y="2730" as="sourcePoint" />
            <mxPoint x="490" y="2730" as="targetPoint" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Y4wUbL-xrpzmWVxsvZfx-20" value="The workout overlay allows users to enter their workout type, duration and date. It is designed to make recording exercise simple and organised by only displaying the fields relevant to workouts. The Save button allows users to submit their information, which can then be stored in the database and used to update their workout history and graph." style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="2735" width="280" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Y4wUbL-xrpzmWVxsvZfx-21" value="The weight overlay allows users to enter their weight and the date it was recorded. This provides a simple way to track changes in weight over time. The Save button stores the information in the database, allowing it to be displayed in the user&#39;s history and weight graph." style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="438" y="3030" width="262" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Y4wUbL-xrpzmWVxsvZfx-22" value="The calories overlay allows users to enter their calories consumed, calories burned and the date. Separating these inputs makes it easier to record calorie information accurately. The Save button stores the data in the database, allowing it to be used in the calories graph and fitness history." style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="990" y="3010" width="270" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Y4wUbL-xrpzmWVxsvZfx-23" value="&lt;div class=&quot;flex max-w-full flex-col gap-4 grow&quot;&gt;&lt;div tabindex=&quot;0&quot; data-turn-start-message=&quot;true&quot; class=&quot;min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal outline-none keyboard-focused:focus-ring [.text-message+&amp;amp;]:mt-1&quot; data-message-model-slug=&quot;gpt-5-6&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot; data-message-id=&quot;e0bb7244-601a-418d-939b-326a0eb3aadd&quot; data-message-author-role=&quot;assistant&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;markdown prose dark:prose-invert wrap-break-word w-full dark markdown-new-styling&quot;&gt;&lt;blockquote data-is-only-node=&quot;&quot; data-is-last-node=&quot;&quot; data-end=&quot;1290&quot; data-start=&quot;1014&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer&quot; data-is-last-node=&quot;&quot; data-end=&quot;1290&quot; data-start=&quot;1016&quot;&gt;The steps overlay allows users to enter their step count and the date. This makes recording daily activity quick and straightforward. The Save button stores the information in the database, allowing it to be displayed on the home page and compared with the user&#39;s step goal.&lt;span class=&quot;PDq2pG_selectionAnchor&quot; aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;z-0 flex min-h-[46px] justify-start&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pointer-events-none -mb-px h-px w-full opacity-0&quot; aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1285" y="2750" width="330" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Y4wUbL-xrpzmWVxsvZfx-30" value="The navigation bar is positioned at the top of the page to provide users with easy access to the main features of the fitness tracker.This makes the application easier to navigate because users can move between different sections" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2230" y="2870" width="210" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Y4wUbL-xrpzmWVxsvZfx-31" value="This input allows users to enter their target number of steps per day. The Save button stores the goal in the database so it can be compared with their daily step count and displayed on the home page." style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1680" y="2850" width="290" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Y4wUbL-xrpzmWVxsvZfx-32" value="This input allows users to enter their target workout duration. The Save button stores the goal in the database, allowing users to compare their actual workout time with their target." style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1340" y="3210" width="220" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Y4wUbL-xrpzmWVxsvZfx-33" value="This input allows users to enter their target weight. The Save button saves the goal to the database so changes in weight can be tracked and compared with the user’s target." style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1510" y="3500" width="220" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Y4wUbL-xrpzmWVxsvZfx-34" value="&lt;div class=&quot;flex max-w-full flex-col gap-4 grow&quot;&gt;&lt;div tabindex=&quot;0&quot; data-turn-start-message=&quot;true&quot; class=&quot;min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal outline-none keyboard-focused:focus-ring [.text-message+&amp;amp;]:mt-1&quot; data-message-model-slug=&quot;gpt-5-6&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot; data-message-id=&quot;17bb8044-2046-4cc2-8b73-1b6aef13687f&quot; data-message-author-role=&quot;assistant&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;markdown prose dark:prose-invert wrap-break-word w-full dark markdown-new-styling&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer&quot; data-is-only-node=&quot;&quot; data-is-last-node=&quot;&quot; data-end=&quot;873&quot; data-start=&quot;658&quot;&gt;This input allows users to enter their target number of calories burned. The Save button stores the goal in the database, allowing users to compare their calories burned with their target and monitor their progress.&lt;span class=&quot;PDq2pG_selectionAnchor&quot; aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;z-0 flex min-h-[46px] justify-start&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pointer-events-none -mb-px h-px w-full opacity-0&quot; aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2040" y="3520" width="300" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Y4wUbL-xrpzmWVxsvZfx-42" value="The navigation bar is positioned at the top of the page to provide users with easy access to the main features of the fitness tracker.This makes the application easier to navigate because users can move between different sections" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="980" y="3416" width="267" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Y4wUbL-xrpzmWVxsvZfx-43" value="This section displays the user’s previous workouts, including the date, workout type and duration. This allows users to review their exercise history and monitor how consistently they are working out." style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="130" y="3775" width="250" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Y4wUbL-xrpzmWVxsvZfx-44" value="This section displays the date, number of steps and daily step goal. This allows users to compare their daily activity with their target and track whether they are meeting their step goals." style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="470" y="4070" width="240" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Y4wUbL-xrpzmWVxsvZfx-45" value="This section displays the date, recorded weight and change in weight. This helps users monitor changes in their weight over time and compare their progress with their weight goal." style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1260" y="3775" width="220" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Y4wUbL-xrpzmWVxsvZfx-46" value="&lt;div class=&quot;flex max-w-full flex-col gap-4 grow&quot;&gt;&lt;div tabindex=&quot;0&quot; data-turn-start-message=&quot;true&quot; class=&quot;min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal outline-none keyboard-focused:focus-ring [.text-message+&amp;amp;]:mt-1&quot; data-message-model-slug=&quot;gpt-5-6&quot; dir=&quot;auto&quot; data-message-id=&quot;5d14b636-118c-484a-8abc-f8dddaa58ed1&quot; data-message-author-role=&quot;assistant&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;markdown prose dark:prose-invert wrap-break-word w-full dark markdown-new-styling&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer&quot; data-is-only-node=&quot;&quot; data-is-last-node=&quot;&quot; data-end=&quot;857&quot; data-start=&quot;660&quot;&gt;This section displays the date, calories burned and calories consumed. This allows users to review their calorie information and understand how their calorie intake compares with the amount burned.&lt;span class=&quot;PDq2pG_selectionAnchor&quot; aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;z-0 flex min-h-[46px] justify-start&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pointer-events-none -mb-px h-px w-full opacity-0&quot; aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1116.5" y="4040" width="247" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
